  "details": "1. Get any avatar with slightly inaccurate proportions\n\n2. Compare the real world floor height with the ingame floor height\n\n3. Spend an entire half hour of you life trying to figure out how to make the ingame floor match the real life floor only to find out that the correct answer is \"it's based on the avatar instead of the actual floor.\" Well how do I fix the avatar? \"Make your own.\" ...I DON'T KNOW HOW TO DO THAT EITHER WHAT DO YOU WANT FROM ME\n\nIn conclusion, this game needs a method of aligning the floor with the ground that doesn't take 3 months of learning how Blender, Unity, and human anatomy / proportions work. Maybe, for example, an \"Align floor with avatar\" toggle that lines the floor up with the guardian boundary floor when disabled?",
